  "stem": "<div class=\"figwrap\"><svg class=\"fig\" viewBox=\"0 0 340 280\" width=\"340\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"two parallel lines cut by a transversal\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:12px\"><line x1=\"20\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"320\" y2=\"80\" stroke=\"#222\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"20\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"320\" y2=\"200\" stroke=\"#222\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"110\" y1=\"260\" x2=\"250\" y2=\"20\" stroke=\"#222\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"72\">ℓ</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"192\">m</text><text x=\"230\" y=\"72\">(3x + 15)°</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"192\">(5x − 25)°</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"222\">y°</text></svg><div class=figcap>Note: Figure not drawn to scale.</div></div>In the figure, line \\(\\ell\\) is parallel to line \\(m\\), and both are intersected by a transversal. The angle marked \\((3x+15)^\\circ\\) and the angle marked \\((5x-25)^\\circ\\) are corresponding angles, each lying above its line and to the right of the transversal. The angle marked \\(y^\\circ\\) lies below line \\(m\\) and to the right of the transversal. What is the value of \\(y\\)?",
  "answer": "105",
  "explain": "Corresponding angles formed by parallel lines are equal: \\(3x+15=5x-25\\), so \\(x=20\\) and each angle is \\(75^\\circ\\). The angle \\(y^\\circ\\) and the \\(75^\\circ\\) angle at line \\(m\\) are adjacent and share the part of \\(m\\) to the right of the transversal; their other sides point in opposite directions along the transversal. So they form a linear pair and are supplementary: \\(y=180-75=105\\).",
